1
00:00:05,920 --> 00:00:09,240
YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!

2
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:39,140
It's time to do

3
00:01:03,540 --> 00:01:04,370
Bakura!

4
00:01:04,453 --> 00:01:05,697
Hey, Bakura, you still up there?

5
00:01:05,780 --> 00:01:07,220
Yes, I'm with Mokuba.

6
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:08,700
He's coming around.

7
00:01:12,460 --> 00:01:13,290
Bakura?

8
00:01:13,740 --> 00:01:14,760
Is he okay?

9
00:01:18,420 --> 00:01:20,280
Yes, Mokuba's fine. Great.

10
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:22,637
So his soul's back in his body, huh?

11
00:01:22,720 --> 00:01:23,661
That's a relief.

12
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:26,797
So, he's really all right? He's fine.

13
00:01:26,880 --> 00:01:28,877
Who would have believed a
pegasus would keep his word?

14
00:01:28,960 --> 00:01:30,500
Yeah, go figure.

15
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:32,565
So, how are you doing, Mokuba?

16
00:01:32,820 --> 00:01:34,657
You feeling up to getting off this island?

17
00:01:34,740 --> 00:01:36,000
Not without Seto.

18
00:01:36,420 --> 00:01:37,900
Where's my big brother?

19
00:01:38,660 --> 00:01:40,425
He's somewhere in this castle.

20
00:01:40,540 --> 00:01:41,370
We'll find him.

21
00:01:41,453 --> 00:01:43,500
I bet he already knows you're safe.

22
00:01:44,100 --> 00:01:45,840
Gotta find...

23
00:01:47,060 --> 00:01:47,890
Mokuba.

24
00:01:48,380 --> 00:01:49,740
Yugi? Joey?

25
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:51,330
Croquet?

26
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:53,160
Due to his illness, Mr.

27
00:01:53,300 --> 00:01:55,241
Pegasus will be unable to attend.

28
00:01:55,740 --> 00:01:56,737
You ask me.

29
00:01:56,820 --> 00:01:59,897
It's just a lame excuse to
avoid paying off on the prizes.

30
00:01:59,980 --> 00:02:02,040
All prizes are still to be awarded.

31
00:02:02,540 --> 00:02:07,011
Yugi has already received his agreed-upon
award of Three Freed Souls, but...

32
00:02:08,820 --> 00:02:11,880
In addition, there's this. What is it?

33
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:14,631
It's a card called The Ties of Friendship.

34
00:02:14,780 --> 00:02:18,486
It's the only one of his kind,
hand-painted by Pegasus himself.

35
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:22,620
I was instructed to deliver
it personally to Yugi Moto.

36
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,520
You are now officially King of Games.

37
00:02:26,300 --> 00:02:28,697
This contains a check for the prize money

38
00:02:28,780 --> 00:02:31,680
won by Yuki and his
duel with Joey Wheeler.

39
00:02:32,480 --> 00:02:33,557
It's all yours, Joey.

40
00:02:33,640 --> 00:02:34,940
Just like I promised.

41
00:02:36,060 --> 00:02:37,500
You're the best, Yuki.

42
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:40,207
Three million dollars, Joey.

43
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:42,280
For your sister's operation.

44
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:44,590
Yeah.

45
00:02:44,673 --> 00:02:48,200
We've been apart for so long, but
now I can save her from going blind.

46
00:02:50,340 --> 00:02:51,480
That's great, Joey.

47
00:02:51,760 --> 00:02:53,020
Yeah, you bet it is.

48
00:02:53,920 --> 00:02:56,020
Now, we'd like you all to leave.

49
00:02:57,360 --> 00:03:01,900
Yugi, I just realized if Mokuba's
soul has been returned, then maybe...

50
00:03:02,440 --> 00:03:05,580
Yeah, it should mean that
Grandpa's recovering too.

51
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,647
I can't wait to get him
out of that hospital.

52
00:03:11,800 --> 00:03:13,720
Yugi, you saved me.

53
00:03:16,340 --> 00:03:17,170
Seto!

54
00:03:17,253 --> 00:03:18,200
Big brother!

55
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:20,530
Seto!

56
00:03:20,613 --> 00:03:22,160
It's me, Mokuba!

57
00:03:23,320 --> 00:03:24,700
Where are you?

58
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:26,580
The castle's huge.

59
00:03:26,700 --> 00:03:28,517
Kaiba could be almost anywhere.

60
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:29,430
Hey!

61
00:03:32,260 --> 00:03:33,320
It's him!

62
00:03:38,020 --> 00:03:39,300
Big Brother!

63
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:42,240
You're here!

64
00:03:42,480 --> 00:03:43,500
You're here!

65
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:45,620
It's all right.

66
00:03:47,860 --> 00:03:49,020
Come on.

67
00:03:49,260 --> 00:03:51,277
Let's not get all mushy
and gooey, you know?

68
00:03:51,360 --> 00:03:52,900
I can't take it.

69
00:03:55,100 --> 00:03:58,320
Oh, Seto, I didn't know
what happened to you.

70
00:03:58,440 --> 00:04:01,322
But I never stopped thinking
of you, big brother.

71
00:04:01,940 --> 00:04:02,770
I know.

72
00:04:04,560 --> 00:04:07,377
I would have risked anything
to save you, Mokuba.

73
00:04:07,460 --> 00:04:09,280
Yugi told me you risked a lot.

74
00:04:09,480 --> 00:04:11,580
And now we're together again, Seto.

75
00:04:11,860 --> 00:04:13,837
So what do you say, little brother?

76
00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:18,180
Ready for me to take you back home
where we both belong? You bet.

77
00:04:19,080 --> 00:04:20,120
Thank you, Yugi.

78
00:04:20,760 --> 00:04:23,289
Thanks for saving my
brother Mokuba's soul.

79
00:04:23,620 --> 00:04:25,117
He means everything to me.

80
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:26,906
How could I do anything else?

81
00:04:27,040 --> 00:04:28,099
And I am grateful.

82
00:04:28,220 --> 00:04:32,573
But because of our circumstances, our
last duel was not really conclusive.

83
00:04:32,900 --> 00:04:33,959
Yes, you're right.

84
00:04:34,460 --> 00:04:36,717
One day we will meet in the arena again to

85
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:39,277
decide which of us is
truly the better duelist.

86
00:04:39,360 --> 00:04:41,713
And one of us will walk away with pride.

87
00:04:42,380 --> 00:04:44,200
Come on, Mokuba. Let's go.

88
00:04:44,560 --> 00:04:45,736
My copter's waiting.

89
00:04:46,240 --> 00:04:47,070
All right!

90
00:04:47,153 --> 00:04:48,080
We're going home!

91
00:04:48,680 --> 00:04:49,600
You did it!

92
00:04:50,520 --> 00:04:52,240
You saved everyone, Yu-Gi.

93
00:04:52,580 --> 00:04:53,520
We both did.

94
00:04:53,740 --> 00:04:55,417
And I don't even know your name.

95
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:57,697
I've been called many
things through the ages.

96
00:04:57,780 --> 00:05:00,800
Pharaoh, Yu-Gi-Oh, I've
been known as Yami.

97
00:05:01,240 --> 00:05:03,828
Well, Yami, I'm proud
to call you my friend.

98
00:05:04,260 --> 00:05:05,090
Good.

99
00:05:05,173 --> 00:05:06,660
Because I'm proud to be one.

100
00:05:08,820 --> 00:05:10,037
I just thought of something.

101
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:11,137
All the boats have left.

102
00:05:11,220 --> 00:05:13,926
So how are we supposed
to get off this island?

103
00:05:14,380 --> 00:05:16,300
We gotta hitch a ride. Come on!

104
00:05:16,480 --> 00:05:18,380
Wait for us, Kaiba! And us too!

105
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:24,500
Yuki has the championship, Joey has
the money, but I hold the real prize.

106
00:05:25,560 --> 00:05:30,400
The Millennium I, and soon, I'll have
Yuki's Millennium puzzled as well.

107
00:05:37,780 --> 00:05:39,192
What's the matter, Yuki?

108
00:05:39,540 --> 00:05:42,658
You're not surprised to see
me up and about, are you?

109
00:05:43,440 --> 00:05:44,270
Grandpa.

110
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:48,137
Hey, Grandpa.

111
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:49,050
You're okay.

112
00:05:49,133 --> 00:05:50,340
Yes, my boy.

113
00:05:53,780 --> 00:05:54,820
I've missed you.

114
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:55,957
Ready to go home?

115
00:05:56,040 --> 00:05:56,870
Mm-hmm.

116
00:05:58,480 --> 00:06:02,940
So you saved me and became champion
of the Duelist Kingdom, Yugi?

117
00:06:03,140 --> 00:06:04,897
I didn't do it alone, Grandpa.

118
00:06:04,980 --> 00:06:06,800
Everyone helped. That's right.

119
00:06:06,940 --> 00:06:08,157
Everybody pitched in.

120
00:06:08,240 --> 00:06:10,593
But he couldn't have done it without me.

121
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:15,560
Well, then you've obviously
improved since I last saw you duel.

122
00:06:15,820 --> 00:06:17,137
Uh, not that much.

123
00:06:17,220 --> 00:06:18,340
Eh, a lot.

124
00:06:18,620 --> 00:06:20,657
Grandpa, maybe you
should go home and rest.

125
00:06:20,740 --> 00:06:22,377
You did just get out of
the hospital, you know?

126
00:06:22,460 --> 00:06:23,290
Don't be silly.

127
00:06:23,373 --> 00:06:24,203
I feel great.

128
00:06:24,286 --> 00:06:27,720
One, two, three, four,
one, two... Grandma!

129
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:29,820
Are you okay, Mr. Moto?

130
00:06:30,180 --> 00:06:32,700
Just a little stiff, that's all. Hey!

131
00:06:33,580 --> 00:06:35,277
I've got something to say to you.

132
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:37,654
That is, if you're who I think you are.

133
00:06:37,880 --> 00:06:40,040
What in the world? Hmm.

134
00:06:40,540 --> 00:06:41,440
Who is that?

135
00:06:41,620 --> 00:06:42,679
You guys know her?

136
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:45,430
Hello?

137
00:06:45,580 --> 00:06:47,639
Tell me, is your name Solomon Moto?

138
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:49,150
That's right.

139
00:06:49,280 --> 00:06:50,600
And who might you be?

140
00:06:50,960 --> 00:06:51,920
Who might I be?

141
00:06:52,100 --> 00:06:53,218
I might be Rebecca.

142
00:06:53,520 --> 00:06:55,737
And I might have just
arrived here in town.

143
00:06:55,820 --> 00:06:58,097
And I might have been
waiting for you to show up.

144
00:06:58,180 --> 00:07:02,577
It's not nice to keep a lady waiting,
you know. A lady? That's right.

145
00:07:02,660 --> 00:07:04,797
Are you saying I'm not a lady, Buster?

146
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:05,720
Wait a minute.

147
00:07:05,940 --> 00:07:08,917
What's a little squirt like you doing
traveling all by yourself anyway?

148
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:10,780
That's dangerous. Oh, yeah?

149
00:07:10,940 --> 00:07:12,197
Well, I can take care of myself.

150
00:07:12,280 --> 00:07:13,997
And if not, I've got Teddy to protect me.

151
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:15,740
Isn't that right, Teddy?

152
00:07:16,100 --> 00:07:17,520
She talks to the bear?

153
00:07:17,900 --> 00:07:18,920
Rebecca, wait.

154
00:07:19,160 --> 00:07:21,137
What exactly is it you want from me?

155
00:07:21,220 --> 00:07:22,260
My card back!

156
00:07:22,520 --> 00:07:23,461
Beg your pardon?

157
00:07:23,780 --> 00:07:25,697
You've got my Blue-Eyes White Dragon.

158
00:07:25,780 --> 00:07:27,540
Now give it back to me! Huh?

159
00:07:28,140 --> 00:07:29,797
Listen, you heard what I said.

160
00:07:29,880 --> 00:07:31,917
I want my Blue-Eyes back right now!

161
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:33,471
There's a slight problem.

162
00:07:39,020 --> 00:07:42,057
The Blue-Eyes White Dragon
is an ultra-rare and powerful

163
00:07:42,140 --> 00:07:45,197
card that only belongs in
the deck of a true champion.

164
00:07:45,280 --> 00:07:47,177
I, Rebecca, am a true champion.

165
00:07:47,260 --> 00:07:51,317
I've traveled the world and beaten
many top duelists while you were away.

166
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:52,812
Isn't that right, Teddy?

167
00:07:53,020 --> 00:07:55,537
You've beaten top
duelists around the world?

168
00:07:55,620 --> 00:07:58,840
Yep, I dare say I'm the
number one duelist in America.

169
00:07:59,200 --> 00:08:01,700
Aren't you a little young? I'm eight.

170
00:08:01,920 --> 00:08:03,080
Yeah, inches tall.

171
00:08:03,260 --> 00:08:05,677
You really shouldn't
tell lies, little girl.

172
00:08:05,760 --> 00:08:07,960
Wait, it may not be a lie.

173
00:08:08,160 --> 00:08:09,777
I remember reading something,

174
00:08:09,860 --> 00:08:11,617
an article just before we left for the

175
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:14,257
duelist kingdom about a
duel monster's prodigy.

176
00:08:14,340 --> 00:08:16,340
She was causing a major sensation.

177
00:08:18,380 --> 00:08:19,210
No way.

178
00:08:19,620 --> 00:08:23,497
You're not telling me this little pipsqueak's
really the national champion, are you?

179
00:08:23,580 --> 00:08:25,680
Get real, Yug. What's the deal?

180
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:28,597
Are you questioning my
dueling credentials, pal?

181
00:08:28,680 --> 00:08:30,197
Hey, don't give me any lip.

182
00:08:30,280 --> 00:08:31,633
I got credentials, too.

183
00:08:31,740 --> 00:08:33,757
Second in the duelist kingdom tournament.

184
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:34,670
That's true,

185
00:08:34,860 --> 00:08:37,797
but on the other hand, you probably
don't know how to spell credentials.

186
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:38,710
Knock it off.

187
00:08:38,793 --> 00:08:40,137
You're supposed to be on my side.

188
00:08:40,220 --> 00:08:41,737
Oh, I know all about that.

189
00:08:41,820 --> 00:08:44,457
First place in the Duelist Kingdom went to

190
00:08:44,540 --> 00:08:48,260
Yugi Moto and second place
went to Joey Wheeler.

191
00:08:48,760 --> 00:08:50,780
But who cares who came in second?

192
00:08:51,100 --> 00:08:53,177
It's only first place that really matters.

193
00:08:53,260 --> 00:08:54,477
Isn't that right, Teddy?

194
00:08:54,560 --> 00:08:55,740
Let me ask her!

195
00:08:56,340 --> 00:08:58,520
But Rebecca, I'm confused.

196
00:08:58,880 --> 00:09:02,977
Why do you think your championship entitles
you to my Blue Eyes White Dragon card?

197
00:09:03,060 --> 00:09:04,413
No, I don't think that.

198
00:09:04,620 --> 00:09:08,457
The Blue Eyes White Dragon card should
be mine because you stole it from me.

199
00:09:08,540 --> 00:09:10,480
Just wait a minute. No way.

200
00:09:10,680 --> 00:09:11,637
My grandfather?

201
00:09:11,720 --> 00:09:12,840
He'd never steal.

202
00:09:13,020 --> 00:09:16,217
Well, there are only four Blue Eyes
White Dragon cards in the world.

203
00:09:16,300 --> 00:09:18,771
Kaiba's got three, and my card is missing.

204
00:09:19,740 --> 00:09:20,975
What's with you, kid?

205
00:09:21,100 --> 00:09:22,917
You're not making any sense here.

206
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:26,397
That Blue Eyes White Dragon is mine,
and if you won't give it back to me,

207
00:09:26,480 --> 00:09:28,717
then I demand the right to duel for it.

208
00:09:28,800 --> 00:09:30,580
Rebecca, you don't understand.

209
00:09:31,700 --> 00:09:32,717
Oh, yes, I do.

210
00:09:32,800 --> 00:09:34,040
Your Grant's scared.

211
00:09:34,260 --> 00:09:35,877
He's just afraid to duel with me.

212
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:36,940
No, no.

213
00:09:37,200 --> 00:09:39,037
He's not afraid to duel you, Rebecca.

214
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:41,800
It's just that that card, it's... well...

215
00:09:42,360 --> 00:09:44,360
I've heard enough of your excuses!

216
00:09:44,800 --> 00:09:46,340
Duel me, old man, now!

217
00:09:47,280 --> 00:09:48,540
Listen, Solomon Moto,

218
00:09:48,860 --> 00:09:52,257
if I win this duel, you give that
blue-eyes white dragon back to me!

219
00:09:52,340 --> 00:09:55,177
What does it take to penetrate
that thick skull of yours?

220
00:09:55,260 --> 00:09:56,090
To the arena!

221
00:09:56,280 --> 00:09:57,680
I will eat you alive!

222
00:10:07,300 --> 00:10:09,960
Look, it's a blue eyes, a real one!

223
00:10:10,160 --> 00:10:12,020
It's just a statue, son.

224
00:10:16,020 --> 00:10:17,240
Hey, all right!

225
00:10:17,440 --> 00:10:18,300
I win again!

226
00:10:18,600 --> 00:10:20,180
I love Kaivaland, sis!

227
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:22,500
So, can you help us, Mokuba?

228
00:10:22,700 --> 00:10:24,229
You're asking a lot, Yugi.

229
00:10:24,760 --> 00:10:28,857
You know, Kaivaland's dual rings are
booked solid for the next three months.

230
00:10:28,940 --> 00:10:31,340
But, of course, we do owe you big time.

231
00:10:31,460 --> 00:10:32,342
Thanks, Mokuba.

232
00:10:32,860 --> 00:10:35,177
Well, so what are we all waiting for?

233
00:10:35,260 --> 00:10:37,360
Let's get this duel on the road.

234
00:10:37,800 --> 00:10:39,020
Nice dueling arena.

235
00:10:39,220 --> 00:10:40,573
A little small, though.

236
00:10:41,820 --> 00:10:43,060
Okay, Mr. Moto.

237
00:10:43,480 --> 00:10:44,840
Are you ready to duel?

238
00:10:45,940 --> 00:10:46,897
But Grandpa...

239
00:10:46,980 --> 00:10:47,960
Relax, Yugi.

240
00:10:48,200 --> 00:10:49,080
I'll be fine.

241
00:10:49,320 --> 00:10:50,180
I don't know.

242
00:10:52,460 --> 00:10:53,600
What is this?

243
00:10:53,740 --> 00:10:56,975
Are we going to duel or settle
in for an afternoon nap?

244
00:10:57,100 --> 00:10:58,220
He can't duel you.

245
00:10:58,440 --> 00:10:59,734
I'll face you instead.

246
00:11:00,380 --> 00:11:01,210
Yugi?

247
00:11:01,293 --> 00:11:03,717
Grandpa was just released from
the hospital this morning.

248
00:11:03,800 --> 00:11:06,357
He's in no condition
to be dueling, Rebecca.

249
00:11:06,440 --> 00:11:08,205
Okay, then that's even better.

250
00:11:08,380 --> 00:11:10,897
Rebecca, the national
champion versus Yugi Moto,

251
00:11:10,980 --> 00:11:13,797
winner of the duelist
kingdom in a clash of titans.

252
00:11:13,880 --> 00:11:16,677
Of course, it's still ordinary
him against genius me,

253
00:11:16,760 --> 00:11:19,777
so he doesn't stand a chance
of winning, does he, Teddy?

254
00:11:19,860 --> 00:11:20,900
Not a chance.

255
00:11:23,180 --> 00:11:26,597
I can't tell if she's just stuck
on herself or totally nuts.

256
00:11:26,680 --> 00:11:27,510
Or maybe both.

257
00:11:27,593 --> 00:11:29,031
You guys watch from here.

258
00:11:29,880 --> 00:11:31,720
Be very careful, Yugi.

259
00:11:31,980 --> 00:11:34,600
She is strange. But smart.

260
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:36,070
Let's duel!

261
00:11:42,640 --> 00:11:46,140
Oh, Yugi, sure you wanna go
through with this? I'm sure.

262
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:49,857
Okay, but it'd be a lot easier just
to give me the blue-eyes white dragon.

263
00:11:49,940 --> 00:11:51,977
You're up against a genius, you know.

264
00:11:52,060 --> 00:11:54,040
Aw, Teddy, isn't that right?

265
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:56,500
Yup, yup, you're a genius, Rebecca.

266
00:11:57,740 --> 00:11:59,460
Now let's get down to it.

267
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:01,857
Who on earth is this young lady?

268
00:12:01,940 --> 00:12:05,352
And why does she think I stole
her blue-eyes white dragon?

269
00:12:05,680 --> 00:12:07,080
It's your turn! Hmm.

270
00:12:08,020 --> 00:12:12,138
For my first brilliant move, Witch
of the Black Forest in attack mode!

271
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:13,310
Alright!

272
00:12:13,393 --> 00:12:15,531
Let's see what you're worth, witchy woman!

273
00:12:18,820 --> 00:12:19,650
Huh.

274
00:12:22,620 --> 00:12:24,880
An unusual opening gambit.

275
00:12:25,460 --> 00:12:26,560
What's she up to?

276
00:12:26,780 --> 00:12:29,817
Witch of the Black Forest isn't
really that strong of a card at all.

277
00:12:29,900 --> 00:12:32,040
Hmm, why would she play that?

278
00:12:32,460 --> 00:12:34,580
He thinks very slowly, Teddy.

279
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:37,235
Do you suppose he'll ever play a card?

280
00:12:37,660 --> 00:12:39,100
I'll play, Rebecca.

281
00:12:39,540 --> 00:12:42,060
The Celtic Guardian in attack mode!

282
00:12:43,080 --> 00:12:45,640
Celtic Guardian, attack the witch!

283
00:12:50,220 --> 00:12:53,240
So much for your Black Forest witch! Whoa!

284
00:12:54,080 --> 00:12:57,660
That mean old Yugi sent my
worthless witch to the graveyard!

285
00:12:57,860 --> 00:12:58,877
Oh, what do I do?

286
00:12:58,960 --> 00:12:59,920
Huh?

287
00:13:00,180 --> 00:13:01,180
What did you say?

288
00:13:01,500 --> 00:13:02,900
Oh, thank you!

289
00:13:03,140 --> 00:13:05,937
If the Witch of the Black
Forest is sent to the graveyard,

290
00:13:06,020 --> 00:13:07,917
I get to pick another card for my deck.

291
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:10,620
A monster with up to 1,500 defense points!

292
00:13:10,960 --> 00:13:14,120
And I get to shuffle my deck again! Whee!

293
00:13:14,520 --> 00:13:15,540
Thank you, Teddy!

294
00:13:23,700 --> 00:13:24,880
Well, I'm waiting.

295
00:13:25,220 --> 00:13:26,497
Are you going to play or what?

296
00:13:26,580 --> 00:13:30,480
Hey, don't you distract me
when I'm faking. What's next?

297
00:13:30,740 --> 00:13:32,622
Decisions, decisions, decisions.

298
00:13:32,900 --> 00:13:35,547
That kid could drive
you crazy really easily.

299
00:13:35,820 --> 00:13:38,000
Oh, I guess I'm stuck with this one.

300
00:13:38,840 --> 00:13:39,781
Hmm, here we go.

301
00:13:41,040 --> 00:13:43,340
I play Sangin in attack mode.

302
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:49,260
Aw, he's so cute, isn't he?

303
00:13:49,700 --> 00:13:50,820
Not for long.

304
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:53,300
You can kiss Sangin goodbye. Oh.

305
00:13:53,760 --> 00:13:55,220
Keldick Guardian attack!

306
00:13:58,880 --> 00:13:59,710
Oh!

307
00:13:59,793 --> 00:14:03,146
That Celtic Guardian sent my poor
Sangin to the graveyard, too!

308
00:14:03,460 --> 00:14:04,660
You're so mean!

309
00:14:04,980 --> 00:14:05,921
Give me a break.

310
00:14:06,320 --> 00:14:09,140
I'm not being mean, I'm
just playing the game.

311
00:14:09,480 --> 00:14:10,877
Did you hear that, Teddy?

312
00:14:10,960 --> 00:14:12,980
Nasty old Yugi is yelling at me!

313
00:14:13,220 --> 00:14:14,880
And I'm not yelling at you!

314
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:16,270
Huh?

315
00:14:16,353 --> 00:14:17,200
What did you say?

316
00:14:17,340 --> 00:14:19,222
We haven't lost just yet, Teddy?

317
00:14:19,460 --> 00:14:22,872
If Sangin goes to the graveyard,
I can pull a new monster?

318
00:14:23,580 --> 00:14:24,410
Mm-hmm.

319
00:14:24,620 --> 00:14:25,860
I understand that.

320
00:14:26,920 --> 00:14:27,780
I don't know.

321
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:29,020
That girl's weird.

322
00:14:29,320 --> 00:14:31,917
Geniuses are supposed to
be eccentric, you know.

323
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:33,057
Come on, you guys.

324
00:14:33,140 --> 00:14:33,970
You gotta be kidding.

325
00:14:34,053 --> 00:14:35,357
That little twerp's no genius.

326
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:36,675
She's just a nutcase.

327
00:14:38,120 --> 00:14:38,950
Hmm.

328
00:14:39,033 --> 00:14:41,440
Rebecca's strategy is
strangely familiar to me.

329
00:14:42,580 --> 00:14:44,420
Now let's get down to business.

330
00:14:44,900 --> 00:14:46,018
Kid gloves are off.

331
00:14:46,160 --> 00:14:47,866
You've met your match, Huggy.

332
00:14:49,500 --> 00:14:51,559
Suddenly, she's a lot more serious.

333
00:14:52,300 --> 00:14:53,860
I play a magic card.

334
00:14:54,040 --> 00:14:54,897
Tribute to the Doom.

335
00:14:54,980 --> 00:14:58,280
It lets me throw away one
card from my own hand.

336
00:14:58,440 --> 00:15:02,911
In exchange, I get to wipe out one of
my opponent's monsters from the field.

337
00:15:04,580 --> 00:15:05,540
Just watch!

338
00:15:11,760 --> 00:15:13,600
Hellcic Guardian went bye-bye!

339
00:15:14,740 --> 00:15:18,269
And to finish my turn, I play
one more card in defense mode.

340
00:15:23,300 --> 00:15:25,777
Here's where things start
to get interesting, Yugi.

341
00:15:25,860 --> 00:15:29,277
Mark my words, the Blue-Eyes
White Dragon will be mine again!

342
00:15:29,360 --> 00:15:33,677
Am I having hallucinations, or did she just
put on a totally different personality?

343
00:15:33,760 --> 00:15:34,590
Uh-uh.

344
00:15:34,673 --> 00:15:36,557
She's a lot smarter than
she led us to believe.

345
00:15:36,640 --> 00:15:38,460
Watch out for her, Yugi! Yeah.

346
00:15:39,360 --> 00:15:40,190
Teya's right.

347
00:15:40,273 --> 00:15:42,337
That little kid stuff was just an act.

348
00:15:42,420 --> 00:15:44,067
Rebecca's a serious duelist.

349
00:15:44,340 --> 00:15:45,317
All right, Rebecca!

350
00:15:45,400 --> 00:15:48,340
I attack with Summon Skull!

351
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:54,100
Big mistake, Yugi!

352
00:15:54,760 --> 00:15:57,540
The card I played was
the Millennium Shield!

353
00:15:57,840 --> 00:15:59,134
The Millennium Shield?

354
00:15:59,300 --> 00:16:03,880
It has 3,000 defense points, and your
skull only has 2,500 attack points!

355
00:16:05,900 --> 00:16:08,480
So you lose 500 life points!

356
00:16:16,940 --> 00:16:17,770
Wee!

357
00:16:17,853 --> 00:16:19,640
Yu-Gi's down 500 points!

358
00:16:19,840 --> 00:16:22,117
Hey, that little sport can actually duel.

359
00:16:22,200 --> 00:16:24,017
Someone's trained her very well.

360
00:16:24,100 --> 00:16:28,159
Wait, I've seen that card before
with its overwhelming defense power.

361
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:29,880
I remember now.

362
00:16:30,340 --> 00:16:32,600
It's called the Millennium Shield.

363
00:16:32,900 --> 00:16:34,488
Interesting card, isn't it?

364
00:16:34,580 --> 00:16:35,840
It certainly is.

365
00:16:36,040 --> 00:16:39,017
Your defense is now
impenetrable, Professor Hawkins.

366
00:16:39,100 --> 00:16:40,880
Arthur, call me Arthur.

367
00:16:41,120 --> 00:16:43,437
It was at an archaeological dig in Egypt

368
00:16:43,520 --> 00:16:46,220
so many years ago that
I'd nearly forgotten,

369
00:16:46,560 --> 00:16:51,820
but almost card for card, my friend Professor
Hawkins and I played this same duel.

370
00:16:52,100 --> 00:16:55,297
Why are you so surprised that
I won that last exchange?

371
00:16:55,380 --> 00:16:57,600
I told you I was a child prodigy.

372
00:16:57,720 --> 00:16:59,700
This duel has been easy so far.

373
00:17:00,120 --> 00:17:01,355
Drop him up, Rebecca.

374
00:17:01,960 --> 00:17:02,790
Right, Teddy.

375
00:17:03,440 --> 00:17:06,160
I play a magic card, Ring of Magnetism.

376
00:17:10,860 --> 00:17:12,660
Now, why would she play that?

377
00:17:13,480 --> 00:17:14,310
Hmm.

378
00:17:14,393 --> 00:17:16,177
Combining it with the
Millennium Shield actually

379
00:17:16,260 --> 00:17:19,201
weakens the shield's
overwhelming defensive power.

380
00:17:19,660 --> 00:17:20,760
Poor Yugi.

381
00:17:21,100 --> 00:17:22,640
He's confused, Teddy.

382
00:17:24,240 --> 00:17:25,560
What's he gonna do?

383
00:17:26,360 --> 00:17:27,190
Nothing.

384
00:17:27,273 --> 00:17:29,460
I'm going to pass this turn. Aha!

385
00:17:29,820 --> 00:17:31,938
He's taking a wait-and-see attitude.

386
00:17:32,120 --> 00:17:34,591
Well, if you can't think of a move, I can!

387
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:36,440
Cannon Soldier, attack mode!

388
00:17:40,380 --> 00:17:42,880
Be very careful, Yugi! Huh?

389
00:17:43,140 --> 00:17:45,300
If she sacrifices a monster next,

390
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:49,117
she can turn Cannon Soldier's assault
directly on Yugi's life points.

391
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:51,117
Yeah, but she's never
gonna get the chance,

392
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:54,497
because Yugi's Summoned Skull is
gonna blow Cannon Soldier away.

393
00:17:54,580 --> 00:17:55,410
Let's hope so.

394
00:17:55,493 --> 00:17:58,244
Otherwise, that soldier
will do a lot of damage.

395
00:17:59,780 --> 00:18:02,320
Summon Skull, attack Cannon Soldier!

396
00:18:02,560 --> 00:18:03,900
Lightning strike!

397
00:18:06,980 --> 00:18:08,060
Waste of energy.

398
00:18:08,400 --> 00:18:10,753
Just watch what happens with his attack.

399
00:18:16,240 --> 00:18:17,070
See?

400
00:18:17,153 --> 00:18:20,537
The Ring of Magnetism draws all your
attacks to my Millennium Shield.

401
00:18:20,620 --> 00:18:21,450
Get it?

402
00:18:21,533 --> 00:18:23,257
While the Ring of Magnetism is in play,

403
00:18:23,340 --> 00:18:27,657
my monsters are all safe, because all
you can attack is my Millennium Shield.

404
00:18:27,740 --> 00:18:30,360
And it's got a defense power of 2,500. Ha!

405
00:18:31,260 --> 00:18:32,380
It's a standoff.

406
00:18:32,660 --> 00:18:34,977
Summoned Skull's attack
power is exactly equal

407
00:18:35,060 --> 00:18:37,017
to the defense power of
her Millennium Shield.

408
00:18:37,100 --> 00:18:40,597
I have to break through that
shield somehow in order to win.

409
00:18:40,680 --> 00:18:42,856
So are you having a good time, Teddy?

410
00:18:43,360 --> 00:18:46,480
Good, cause this duel's
gonna get even better now!

411
00:18:49,640 --> 00:18:51,800
Oh cool, it's the Shadow Ghoul.

412
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:55,000
This little baby will come
in handy a little later.

413
00:18:55,320 --> 00:19:00,144
But for now, let's summon another Whippy
Witch of the Black Forest in attack mode!

414
00:19:01,480 --> 00:19:02,620
So long, Witch!

415
00:19:02,780 --> 00:19:05,897
You get used as a sacrifice
to my cannon soldier so he

416
00:19:05,980 --> 00:19:09,098
can turn all his power
directly on Yugi's life point!

417
00:19:10,980 --> 00:19:13,080
Cannon Fulcher, you got her energy.

418
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:14,560
Now blow Yu-Gi away!

419
00:19:22,360 --> 00:19:24,177
Well, that took you down a peg.

420
00:19:24,260 --> 00:19:26,080
Four hundred pegs to be exact.

421
00:19:26,600 --> 00:19:28,659
And now I get to draw another card.

422
00:19:30,020 --> 00:19:31,040
She's real good.

423
00:19:31,300 --> 00:19:34,657
She must have learned dueling from
somebody as experienced as you, Gramps.

424
00:19:34,740 --> 00:19:36,100
Joey, you may be right.

425
00:19:36,700 --> 00:19:37,530
Hmm.

426
00:19:37,613 --> 00:19:41,037
I was taught by someone more
talented than a moto could ever be.

427
00:19:41,120 --> 00:19:43,532
My grandfather was the best duelist ever.

428
00:19:43,820 --> 00:19:44,820
Your grandfather?

429
00:19:45,080 --> 00:19:46,560
Is what I suspect true?

430
00:19:46,760 --> 00:19:49,520
Rebecca, what's your last name?

431
00:19:50,060 --> 00:19:51,920
Took you long enough to ask.

432
00:19:52,500 --> 00:19:55,100
Yes, my name is Rebecca Hawkins.

433
00:19:55,540 --> 00:19:58,460
And my grandfather is
Professor Arthur Hawkins,

434
00:19:58,660 --> 00:20:03,425
the man whose blue-eyes white dragon you
stole and whose friendship you betrayed.

435
00:20:03,580 --> 00:20:04,410
That's crazy.

436
00:20:04,560 --> 00:20:05,390
Absolutely nuts.

437
00:20:05,473 --> 00:20:06,694
You're wrong, Rebecca.

438
00:20:06,880 --> 00:20:09,277
My grandfather would
never betray a friend.

439
00:20:09,360 --> 00:20:10,637
That's what you think.

440
00:20:10,720 --> 00:20:12,917
But your grandfather is a thief, Yugi.

441
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:16,140
He stole my grandfather's
blue-eyes, white dragon.

442
00:20:16,580 --> 00:20:18,160
And you're gonna pay.
